WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.300
Elena reviews a life insurer formed in Pennsylvania and authorized to

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.200
operate in Maryland. Its shareholders own the company.

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.400
Is it stock, foreign, or admitted?
It can be all three.

5
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.100
Stock describes ownership. Foreign describes where the company was formed

6
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:25.700
relative to Maryland. Admitted describes authorization in Maryland.

7
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.080
Exam questions often put these separate dimensions together.

8
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.200
Begin by asking which dimension the question actually tests.

9
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:41.020
A company's location, ownership and permission to transact business are

10
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:46.198
not interchangeable labels. A stock insurer is owned by shareholders.

11
00:00:47.278 --> 00:00:50.838
A mutual insurer is owned by its policyholders, with rights determined

12
00:00:50.838 --> 00:00:52.458
by its structure and law.

13
00:00:53.258 --> 00:00:56.498
Assessment arrangements may permit additional assessments of members under

14
00:00:56.498 --> 00:01:00.818
their terms; do not assume that every mutual policy allows an

15
00:01:00.818 --> 00:01:05.238
extra assessment. Fraternal benefit societies are membership organizations

16
00:01:05.238 --> 00:01:09.758
organized around a common bond and operate under special laws.

17
00:01:10.518 --> 00:01:13.078
They can provide insurance benefits to members.

18
00:01:13.898 --> 00:01:18.058
Private insurers differ from government programs, whose eligibility and

19
00:01:18.058 --> 00:01:21.158
benefits come from their governing laws and program rules.

20
00:01:21.876 --> 00:01:24.776
Domicile refers to the jurisdiction of formation.

21
00:01:26.096 --> 00:01:29.956
For a Maryland question, an insurer formed in Maryland is domestic.

22
00:01:31.096 --> 00:01:32.856
One formed in another U.S.

23
00:01:33.116 --> 00:01:37.976
state is foreign. One formed outside the United States is alien.

24
00:01:38.936 --> 00:01:42.096
These terms say nothing by themselves about whether the company is

25
00:01:42.096 --> 00:01:47.216
licensed in Maryland. A foreign or alien insurer can

26
00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:51.676
be admitted. An office in Baltimore does not turn a Pennsylvania

27
00:01:51.676 --> 00:01:54.896
corporation into a Maryland domestic insurer.

28
00:01:56.016 --> 00:02:00.816
The formation jurisdiction, rather than the producer's office, controls this

29
00:02:00.816 --> 00:02:05.986
classification. An admitted insurer holds authority to

30
00:02:05.986 --> 00:02:09.746
transact the authorized insurance business in the state.

31
00:02:10.526 --> 00:02:13.606
Nonadmitted means it lacks that authority.

32
00:02:14.826 --> 00:02:18.986
This is not a shortcut for placing ordinary life insurance with

33
00:02:18.986 --> 00:02:24.326
any unlicensed company. Verify the insurer and the producer's

34
00:02:24.506 --> 00:02:25.926
authority for the transaction.

35
00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:32.206
Financial-strength ratings are opinions from rating organizations, not

36
00:02:32.206 --> 00:02:35.266
government promises that every benefit will be paid.

37
00:02:36.066 --> 00:02:41.546
Ratings, capital, earnings and operating results can

38
00:02:41.546 --> 00:02:46.786
change. Guaranty protection is a separate statutory system with eligibility

39
00:02:46.786 --> 00:02:50.726
rules, exclusions and limits.

40
00:02:51.672 --> 00:02:54.872
Insurers distribute coverage through several systems.

41
00:02:55.472 --> 00:03:00.892
Captive or exclusive producers generally represent one insurer or

42
00:03:00.892 --> 00:03:06.112
an affiliated group. Independent producers can represent multiple insurers,

43
00:03:06.532 --> 00:03:09.452
subject to their contracts and appointments.

44
00:03:10.392 --> 00:03:16.032
Direct-response distribution can use the internet, mail or telephone without

45
00:03:16.032 --> 00:03:17.992
the same producer relationship.

46
00:03:18.792 --> 00:03:23.552
The label independent does not mean authority to bind every insurer.

47
00:03:24.712 --> 00:03:28.872
A purchasing group is a group formed to buy insurance; it

48
00:03:28.872 --> 00:03:31.112
is not automatically an insurer.

49
00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:36.712
Federal risk purchasing groups chiefly concern liability insurance,

50
00:03:37.292 --> 00:03:41.572
so do not use that label as an ordinary life-placement exception.

51
00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.470
Return to Elena's Pennsylvania company.

52
00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:51.110
It is foreign relative to Maryland, stock because shareholders

53
00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:55.330
own it, and admitted because Maryland has authorized it.

54
00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:00.630
If a rating organization gives it a strong rating, that adds

55
00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:06.630
an opinion about financial strength, not another

56
00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:11.930
type of license. If a producer represents the company, check

57
00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.970
that producer's authority separately.

58
00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:20.810
Keep five questions distinct: who owns the insurer, where

59
00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:26.090
was it formed, where may it operate, how does it distribute

60
00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:30.210
coverage, and what do current financial measures show?
